the shorthands, and there is no flag that changes them:
                                        \w  \d  \s
U+0041 LATIN CAPITAL LETTER A           yes no  no
U+00E9 LATIN SMALL LETTER E WITH ACUTE  no  no  no
U+0301 COMBINING ACUTE ACCENT           no  no  no
U+0660 ARABIC-INDIC DIGIT ZERO          no  no  no
U+FF11 FULLWIDTH DIGIT ONE              no  no  no
U+00A0 NO-BREAK SPACE                   no  no  no
U+3000 IDEOGRAPHIC SPACE                no  no  no

the Unicode categories, which is all RE2 offers:
                                        \pL     \p{Nd}  \p{Zs}
U+0041 LATIN CAPITAL LETTER A           yes     no      no
U+00E9 LATIN SMALL LETTER E WITH ACUTE  yes     no      no
U+0301 COMBINING ACUTE ACCENT           no      no      no
U+0660 ARABIC-INDIC DIGIT ZERO          no      yes     no
U+FF11 FULLWIDTH DIGIT ONE              no      yes     no
U+00A0 NO-BREAK SPACE                   no      no      yes
U+3000 IDEOGRAPHIC SPACE                no      no      yes

RE2 has no binary Unicode properties -- ERR means "failed to compile":
  \p{White_Space}   ERR
  \p{Alphabetic}    ERR
  \p{Word}          ERR

\b\w+\b over 'na' U+00EF 've reader' -- how many words?
  \b\w+\b          -> 3   na ve reader
  \b[\pL\pN_]+\b   -> 2   na\u00EFve reader

\d and the number that follows it (subject is U+0660 U+0661 U+0662):
  \d+          -> no
  \p{Nd}+      -> yes
  strconv.Atoi -> error
